good idea but the only server with people on just kind of run around in one spot all together and pvp eachother, so you have this big hectic gathering of all species just jumping around, no real survival element unfortunately otherwise it might be more fun
{edit} 
server is pretty fun now but game is a broken buggy mess so review remains negative

Finally a new SAO game that plays like Fatal Bullet (FB). That is, as long as you play a character that uses a gun, as his main weapon.

[b]The good[/b]:
+ Fun gameplay, with some depth to it;
+ Tons of characters to choose from and play as;
+ Long story. The devs said it takes 20 hours to complete. Took me 50+;
+ Fun coop experience;
+ Huge roster of characters to play as.

[b]The bad[/b]:
- Always online and an anticheat. I don't have a huge problem with that, but not everyone is going to like it;
- Lack of extra singleplayer content (you do get some tower thingy, once you finish the game, but I wish there was more);
- Fairly steep price atm;
- Seems kinda grindy;
- In-game monetization;
- Currently there's not many maps/bosses to fight.
- Various connectivity issues/bugs

[b]How it compares to FB[/b]:
I'd say it's an overall better game than FB. Though, currently, FB has more singleplayer content, BUT FD is still a brand new game, so you gotta cut it some slack.

i was debating whether i wanted to play this game or not for awhile after learning about it from a friend of mine, but decided to go ahead and give it a shot. i work night shifts so i decided to download it to my steam deck for portability. steam says its incompatible, but after installing the latest photon ge it works perfectly. you have to play at the lowest graphical settings, otherwise the deck over heats, but so far i havent had any major issues with it.

as of writing this review i have 40+ hours and my main class is level 65. i havent been the most efficient with my leveling, tbh, so im sure others can be further along by now than i am. ^~^;

tldr; the game is a lot of fun to play, even on the steam deck (you need photon ge to play it on deck, however)

[h1] SCORN REVIEW [/h1]

A few years ago, i was just browsing youtube when i first saw this game, it seemed very promising since it sold the idea of a immersive FPS horror fleshy ambiented game, like [i]DOOM[/i] but with a slow pace, i whislisted it and waited like... 4 years to launch it? And when finally i bought it, it was not what i expected.


[u] Pros [/u]

1. Very interesting atmosphere;
2. Textures are beaultiful and well mixed with enviroment; 
3. Gameplay is smooth and despite some visual issues, bugs are quite non-existent;
4. Combat is challenging enough (despite the fact that you can avoid almost all of them);
5. Gore, for those who like it;
6. Satisfying mechanics in a certain way.

[u] Cons [/u]

1. Easy puzzles, the hardest being the first one, leading you to dissatisfaction for solving them;
2. Lack of music, which isn't necessarily bad but the game environment feels empty;
3. Fails in being horror genre or create any kind of tension;
4. Repetitive and boring combat because almost all enemies simply spit on you;
5. Short game. Basically the hours you spent are passed by exploring mazes the game keep throwing at you with without any clue to what to do with a bunch of enemies to deal with, plus the puzzles you need to solve;
6. Unintuitive gameplay and lore, and no tutorial at all;
7. Not much gore, only few times in cutscenes and when killing a specific type of enemy with a specific gun;
8. Slow animations when interacting with "panels", and there's a lot of them.


[h1] CONCLUSION [/h1]

The game sold an pretty much different idea of what it truly are, there are various issues in the attempt to reach the wanted genre in this game and it ended up making this game looking more like a cozy puzzle game with horror ambience and occasional combat than a horror game with tense fights and some puzzles. But at all this game can still be good in it's own terms.

Said that, i'm still gonna downvote this game because of the expectations it created and not fullfiled but you can upvote the game if you're aware of it truly nature.

[b] MY VEREDICT: [/b] Wait for a good discount and buy this game.

I hated every second of playing this game. 

p.s. we will always miss you Jovita ;--; 

